[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966866003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116758#issuecomment-3966866003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116758","id":3966866003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7scZJT","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T14:08:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T14:08:42Z","body":"I wouldn't call this a false positive. The result of `<MyEnum> + <MyEnum>` is an `int` value, not `MyEnum`. Because enum values ​​typically don't span all possible `int` values. Yes, we can validate this for constant expressions, but we can't validate it for variables, and I wouldn't call this a well-defined operation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966866003/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967072218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116758#issuecomment-3967072218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116758","id":3967072218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sdLfa","user":{"login":"AidasLit","id":129107308,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7IFbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129107308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit","html_url":"https://github.com/AidasLit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T14:42:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T14:42:30Z","body":"To my knowledge, the ``+=`` operator is the exact same as ``property = property + value``, unless I got this definition wrong. If they're the same, then either the warning should show up on both, or on neither. I'm not really arguing for enabling or disabling the warning for such an operation, but the inconsistency between what should be the exact same code. Do correct me if my understanding here is wrong though, I don't know much about how the code handles ``+=`` internally.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967072218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967189363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116758#issuecomment-3967189363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116758","id":3967189363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sdoFz","user":{"login":"AidasLit","id":129107308,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7IFbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129107308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit","html_url":"https://github.com/AidasLit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T15:02:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T15:02:27Z","body":"Ok looking at it again, I think I see where my confusion comes from.\n\n<img width=\"304\" height=\"57\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f8ed0ae-e1a0-4bd8-aabf-e2f7aa7e2f8f\" />\n\nThe image should explain it, it's a scoping thing. Using ``+=`` uses the scoping on the bottom line, so it throws a warning just like here. I'm more so confused why ``as`` is applying to the whole sum instead of only the number though. The docs don't seem to mention the scoping rules for casting, so I don't know what's the intended behaviour here. Shouldn't the type casting apply only to the number, not the sum expression?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967189363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967233817","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116758#issuecomment-3967233817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116758","id":3967233817,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sdy8Z","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T15:09:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T15:09:17Z","body":"> The docs don't seem to mention the scoping rules for casting, so I don't know what's the intended behaviour here.\n\nSee the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#operators). The `as` operator has lower precedence than the binary `+` operator. The `as` operator has almost the lowest precedence, except for the assignment operators.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967233817/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967312172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116758#issuecomment-3967312172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116758","id":3967312172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7seGEs","user":{"login":"AidasLit","id":129107308,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7IFbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129107308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit","html_url":"https://github.com/AidasLit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AidasLit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T15:21:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T15:21:22Z","body":"> See the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#operators). The `as` operator has lower precedence than the binary `+` operator. The `as` operator has almost the lowest precedence, except for the assignment operators.\n\nMissed that part, sorry. Personally it seems like a confusing placement for the type casting, it allows for an expression like\n```gdscript\nvar a = 5.9 as float if true else 6 as int\n```\nto cast the float as int and throw a warning. Maybe it's just a byproduct of the type casting operator being an actual word like ``and``, ``or``, etc. but I'm no operator precedence designer. Closing the issue, things are working as intended. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967312172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]